  "id": "Compound::DB00298 - Gene::146",
  "verbalization": "Dapiprazole is likely to interact with Adra1d through a shared pathway involving adrenergic receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Dapiprazole binds to Adra1a, which then participates in adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately being participated by Adra1d. This indicates a potential functional link where Dapiprazole may influence Adra1d through its interaction with Adra1a, which is a key component of the adrenergic signaling system. The varying scores across the paths suggest some degree of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains partially inferred. The observed participation of Adra1d in adrenergic receptor activity implies that Dapiprazole may modulate this pathway, potentially through Adra1a, thereby influencing the function of Adra1d.",
